Updates for version 1.260115-U

-- Primarily internal updates, code improvements, changing approaches

New / Changed functionality for version 1.260105-U

 - Targets can (finally) be set by right clicking from chat, etc. (e.g., not just inventory)
   Changed the way targets are set in GUI (GUI equivalent of "/set target *item* *nnn*").
   New approach extends functionality beyond inventory slots and uses a GUI pop up to capture the count  
   instead of seeing the command line.  This is new code which seems to work but I'm not yet 
   extending it to the set targettype" command (partly because I am not convinced I know how to
   get the item type when not using inventory slots as starting points.)
   
 - Expanded / improved the daily endeavors hint command ("/ft hints [keyword]") to include more entries
   The list is still pretty thin but can be easliy expanded now by editing Hints.lua and /reloadui

 - Added a "Reset Panel Positions" button in the GUI (in the miscellaneous Behaviors configuration window) 
   This will reset positions of both farming panels (based on feedback from players who  
   moved the window out of the way [ off screen] and then couldn't get it to move back.)  
   
   
   
Bug Fixes / Corrections
 
 - Changed the way large text blocks are sent to to the chat window (PChat included).  Previously,
   large blocks occassionally required the chat window to be adjusted (e.g., resized) before the buffered 
   entries showed.  New approach seems to fix that.  
   Note: Output still goes to FTK channel if one exists, main chat otherwise. 
   
 - Reordered the loading of script.lua per Baertram's recommendation as well as other moniro changes in the manifest.
   Second upload posted at 6:30 PM PST 260115 without rolling the revision.  
  
