New functionality for version 1.241113-Q 

- By request (WolfGangWag, et al - thank you!), FTK can now also track farming by object type (Fish, Herb, Raw Material, etc.)
  This is in addition to the anmed item level tracking but will be added to the same screen space

  /ft setTypeTarget [type] command allows you to add a type (Fish, Raw Material, Herb, Raw Material, etc.) to the Farming / Shopping list.

  This will track items of type XXX and be shown at the bottom of the farming target list, shows up in the chat's "show targetlist" and saves / loads the data as part of the SaveTargetlist and LoadTargetlist commands.

  So, for your question, you could issue: /ft setTypeTarget Fish 30 and it would put the count on the screen until you has landed 30 fish (from the time you set the target)

  Similar to the setTarget command, setTypeTarget allows you to set a number, "delete" to delete and have a 0 entry for reporting only.

  After testing and feedback, additional changes and updates include:

    - Added a minor wildcard ability such that an entry like #Runestone# will match types of "Potency Runestone", "Essence Runestone", and "Aspect Runestone" entries.
    - Added the ability to right click an item in your inventory to choose "set Type Target" (similar to the functionality for setting targets)
    - Added "/ft resettypetargets" that will zero out the current counts of item types (does not affect the ist of the individual item counts, just the "type" counts)
    - Made the comparisons case insensitive (b/c setTypeTarget herb wasn't working because the type was Herb...)
    - Started to make Herb and Herbs both match but decided I was being too picky.
    - Added new targettypecount table to saved variables so "/ft savetargets" and "/ft loadtargets" now include the type target trackign as well 
      (I've toyed with storing the progress as well as just the targets, not sure I like that though so it is still in progress... feedback welcome)


  Everything is an extension of the farming list so the GUI config controls all cover it.  This includes supporting the "abbreviated" mode on screen


- Added information to Companion code (the part that lists Likes/Dislikes when summoning or returning)
  - Added a new line "Buffs" since the new companions have distinct advantages (Heavy Sack detection for one, lock picking on another, etc.) 

Improved Functionality

  - Added support for new companions (listing when called, likes, dislikes,e tc.)

  - Etended gtr (guild trader review) functionality to bank (to scan bank instead of bags, use /ft gtrb - all the other arguments apply)

Bug Fixes / Corrections
   - Fixed various cases where tables aren't being initialized before use, mostly checks and patches - still hunting what's suddenly going on 
   - Improved readability of type tracking in chat window
   - Improved execution times by removing (commenting out) a lot of debug code.  
     dft_debug won't show anythign unless debugging is turned on but there is still a subroutine call/return which adds to overhead

